course: dictionary
lesson: 8910
title: Shyness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shyness is the feeling of being nervous and quiet with people you do not know well, or when everyone is looking at you. It is a feeling, so it is a noun. You cannot count it, so you say some shyness, not three shynesses.
explain: Shyness is normal. Many people feel shy, even grown-ups, and it can get easier with small brave steps, such as saying hello to one person first. In stories, a shy character may overcome shyness, which means they gradually manage to do the thing they feared.
explain: Look at the words around shyness for clues. You will often see quiet, nervous or hid behind near it. Phrases to notice are «out of shyness», «get over your shyness» and «overcome shyness». Try swapping in nervousness and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Shyness is a noun, and it is uncountable.
fact: «Shyness» means the feeling of being nervous, quiet and uncomfortable with people you don't know well or when everyone is looking at you.
fact: You can say «overcome shyness», «out of shyness» or «get over your shyness».
fact: «Shucks!» is an old-fashioned American mild word used instead of a rude word, and it can show disappointment or shyness.
fact: Many people feel shy, and it can get easier with small brave steps.
exercise: What is shyness? | A type of hat worn in the snow | A kind of loud, bouncy happiness | *A feeling of being nervous and quiet around people you don't know well | A sleepy tiredness after lunch
exercise: «Mia wanted to speak up, but out of shyness she stayed quiet.» Why did Mia stay quiet? | Because she was fast asleep | *Because she felt nervous | Because she was laughing loudly | Because she was angry with her friends
exercise: Which phrase means beating your shyness little by little? | *overcome shyness | count your shyness | share your lunch | lose your shoes
test: Ravi says, «I felt shy at the new club, but I said hello to one girl.» What small brave step did Ravi take? | Leaving the club early | Shouting at everyone | *Saying hello to one person | Hiding behind the door
test: Which word in this list is a noun for a feeling? | shyly | shy about | hide | *shyness
exam: Lena says, «Many people feel shy, so it is normal.» What does this tell you about shyness? | It means being rude | *It is a normal feeling that many people share | It only happens to babies | It is rare and strange
